course: dictionary
lesson: 13494
title: Illuminated: lit up and made clear
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Illuminated means lit up with light. Use the context to check. «The candle illuminated her face, so we could see her smile.» A candle gives light, so illuminated must mean lit up. Swap in lit up and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Illuminated can also mean made clear and easier to understand. «The teacher's diagram illuminated how the heart pumps blood.» A diagram cannot give out light, so here the word means the idea became clear.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Light words such as candle, lamp, moon and sign point to lit up. Words about learning or understanding, such as diagram, explained and clear, point to made clear.
fact: Illuminated means lit up with light.
fact: Illuminated can also mean made clear and easier to understand.
fact: An illuminated manuscript is an old handwritten book decorated with gold, silver and bright colours.
fact: Illuminate is the verb, illuminated is its past form, and illuminating is the form with -ing.
fact: In science, we see an object because light bounces off it after a light source has illuminated it.
exercise: «The street was brightly illuminated by the new lamps.» What does illuminated mean? | Dirty and grey | *Lit up with light | Hidden from view | Covered in snow
exercise: «The diagram illuminated how the heart pumps blood.» What does illuminated mean here? | Painted with gold | Switched off | Broken into pieces | *Made clear and easier to understand
exercise: Monks made an illuminated manuscript. What is it? | *An old handwritten book decorated with gold and bright colours | A new computer game | A map of the sea | A lamp made of glass
test: «The moon illuminated the sleeping town.» Which word is closest in meaning to illuminated? | Shaken | Cleaned | *Lit up | Darkened
test: Which sentence uses illuminated to mean made clear? | «The lamp illuminated the dark hall.» | «The river illuminated under the bridge.» | *«The talk illuminated the causes of the war.» | «The cat illuminated the mat.»
exam: «The sign was illuminated, so drivers could read it at night.» What does illuminated mean here? | Made of wood | *Lit up so it could be seen | Hidden in the dark | Very noisy
